  "rationale": "structural: The text, \"In a design session with no code to write, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to stop after the requirements commit\", sets no library, type, signature, algorithm or delegation obligation. It constrains only what the skill document tells agents, which is observable content. Any wording or structure of the skill that tells agents to stop after the requirements commit satisfies it, so how the skill is organized is discretionary. The supplied root `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` does carry the direction. In `section[Habeas%20requirements]/section[Workflow]/paragraph@739a3f576341`, the requirements-commit step ends with \"In a design session with no code to write, stop here.\" No structural obligation needs further implementation evidence.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one behavioral obligation. In a design session with no code to write, the `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to stop after the requirements commit.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_stops_after_the_commit_in_a_design_session]` covers it and carries the `{test}` marker.\n\n- **Finding the commit step:** the test uses `step_of` to find the Workflow step of `habeas-requirements` that contains \"all groups together\". That phrase is in the commit step (step 5 in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`). `step` then returns that step's text.\n- **Whitespace:** `workflow_steps` joins the step's continuation lines and collapses whitespace. This means the line-wrapped phrase \"design session\\n with no code to write\" can still match.\n- **Assertions:** `assert_text_in_order` requires \"then commit it\" and, after it, \"In a design session with no code to write, stop here\" to appear in that step. The first phrase marks the commit and the second is the stop directive. The test therefore checks both the design-session condition and the instruction to stop at the commit, and it checks that the stop comes after the commit.\n\nI found no untested obligation, boundary or failure case. A step that dropped or moved the stop sentence, or put it before the commit, would fail this test.",
